      "text": "k0t (also CryptoFeel, Member19, QazWsxShop) is a financially motivated cybercriminal actor, first seen on 22 October 2025, behind a large-scale campaign against exposed network edge devices, according to a joint investigation by Group-IB and NyxLab published in October 2026. The actor finds targets by mass enumeration with FOFA and ZoomEye rather than by researching specific organizations. It gains access by exploiting known flaws such as CVE-2025-64446 (FortiWeb) and CVE-2026-0257 (PAN-OS/Prisma Access) with custom Python scripts, or by brute-forcing Fortinet FortiGate and Palo Alto GlobalProtect appliances, then connects over OpenConnect VPN. Post-exploitation relies on NetExec, Impacket,..."
